From deda3b6435b75ef5c23351581d34a1941a13944c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:28:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 25/60] Server: SIGTERM / SIGINT drains before stopping.

New generation requests get 503 with Retry-After (code server_restarting;
Anthropic overloaded_error) and /health answers "draining" without asking the
engine. Requests in progress get TF_DRAIN_S seconds (default 20; a second
signal cuts it short), then the engine's optional halt ends its rounds at a
boundary and what is left fails with "server restarting: retry shortly". The
engine closes before the server is freed, once.

(cherry picked from commit 2c4d837bd01cba152ac66aae74c5eb8d635c6f07)
